// Issue #54. The stat sheet's Movement Speed is published
// as ONE aura, because the core takes the largest
// SPELL_AURA_MOD_INCREASE_SPEED and not the sum: a per-source aura
// would drop every source but the biggest. The module fills the amount
// in from the sheet, whole percent, the same way it fills in the gear
// cost and cooldown reductions.
inline constexpr uint32_t MovementAggregate = 82408;
// The elite-affix slows, as the stock negative aura, so the core
// combines them with the aggregate itself. ONE RECORD PER AFFIX:
// the player is shown this one, and a debuff
// has to say which affix put it there, so the record's name is the
// affix's. Two elites with the SAME affix are still one spell id from
// two casters, which is what SPELL_ATTR3_DOT_STACKING_RULE on each of
// these records is for; separate ids only separate different affixes.
struct AffixSlow { uint32_t id; char const* affix; };
